## 8. Departmental Minutes Editor

This is the core feature of the entire application.

Inside each meeting, provide a departmental minutes editor that supports multiple departments and unlimited agenda items.

Each agenda item must include the following fields:

1. Department — selectable dropdown.
2. Topic / Agenda Item — text input.
3. Discussion / Details — rich multiline text editor.
4. Decision / Resolution — separate field.
5. Action Required — detailed action description.
6. Responsible Person(s) — multi-select employee dropdown.
7. Date Assigned — default to the meeting date.
8. Due Date — date picker.
9. Status — selectable dropdown.
10. Priority — Low, Medium, High, Critical.
11. Additional Notes — optional.
12. Attachments — optional supporting documents.
13. Created By — authenticated user.
14. Last Updated — automatically maintained timestamp.

Allow users to add, edit, delete, and reorder agenda items according to their permissions.

Provide an **Add Agenda Item** button and an **Add Another Department** action.

An agenda item must not be limited to one action or one responsible person. Allow multiple action items when a discussion produces several distinct tasks.

### Department filtering

Provide a department selector at the top of the meeting detail page.

When a user selects Finance, display only the Finance agenda items for that meeting. When the user selects HR, display HR items, and so on.

Include an All Departments option.

Changing the department filter must not delete, modify, or recreate any data.

Also provide a date selector to navigate directly to another meeting and a clear indication of the currently selected meeting date.

### Departmental layout

Use a clean, readable layout that supports both table view and detailed card view.

The table should contain:

Department | Topic | Discussion / Decision | Action Required | Responsible Person | Due Date | Status

Allow users to expand each row to see the full discussion and action details.

Support long text without cutting off important content.

