## 23. Acceptance Criteria

The application is only considered complete when the following requirements have been verified:

1. A user can log in and access the appropriate pages for their role.
2. An authorized user can create a meeting using a date picker.
3. A single meeting can contain multiple departments and agenda items.
4. Each agenda item supports a topic, discussion, decision, actions, assignees, deadlines, and status.
5. Selecting a meeting date displays the correct historical meeting.
6. Filtering by department displays only matching agenda items.
7. Records remain available after refreshing the browser.
8. An unfinished action can be followed up in a later meeting without losing its original history.
9. Search, filters, and status updates work against real data.
10. The uploaded Excel workbook can be parsed, previewed, and imported without silently losing meaningful records.
11. Imported meeting dates, attendees, departments, discussions, responsibilities, and statuses match the source workbook.
12. Users can export a selected meeting to a properly formatted PDF and Excel file.
13. Reports calculate actual values from the database.
14. Unauthorized users cannot bypass permissions through direct database access.
15. Errors, loading states, and empty states are handled correctly.
16. All required pages, buttons, and navigation paths are functional.
17. The application can be configured, deployed, and used by authorized ABSS employees.

